      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's start by substituting the value of $b+d$ into the given equation. We have:\n\n\\[\nab + bc + cd + da = 30\n\\]\n\nSubstitute $b+d = 5$ into the equation:\n\n\\[\nab + bc + cd + da = 30\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out $b$ and $d$ from the terms involving $b$ and $d$:\n\n\\[\nab + bc + cd + da = b(a+c) + d(a+c)\n\\]\n\nFactor out $a+c$:\n\n\\[\nb(a+c) + d(a+c) = (a+c)(b+d)\n\\]\n\nSince $b+d = 5$, we substitute this value in:\n\n\\[\n(a+c)(b+d) = (a+c) \\cdot 5\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n5(a+c) = 30\n\\]\n\nNow, divide both sides by 5:\n\n\\[\na+c = \\frac{30}{5} = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $a+c$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
